meta {
  name: Stop playing
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/me/sessions/{{sessionId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "endDate": "2026-08-18",
    "rating": "Perfect"
  }
}

docs {
  Closes an open session, optionally rating the game in the same transaction so a
  rate-on-stop can never half-land.

  The session id comes from `openSessionId` on the game, which rides along in the
  public read payload precisely so the owner UI can close a session without an
  extra fetch.

  `rating` follows the same PATCH rules as everywhere: omitted leaves it unchanged,
  `""` or `null` clears it.

  Like the two above, this returns the GAME rather than the session.

  - 200 the game, no longer currently playing
  - 404 session nonexistent or under someone else's game
  - 409 session already closed
  - 422 endDate before the session's start date
  - 429 over the write budget
}
